# Run logs are noise; the JSON/JSONL outputs carry the results.
results/*.log

# Raw experiment outputs are IGNORED WHILE IN FLIGHT and committed with
# `git add -f` only once their run has finished. A truncated JSONL is
# indistinguishable from a complete one once it is in git history, and a
# partial experiment file is exactly the kind of artifact that gets cited
# later as if it were the full run.
#
# On completion:  git add -f experiments/results/interventions_raw*.jsonl
results/interventions_raw*.jsonl
